From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:33:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] game.py: split DM_GAMES_DIR on os.pathsep, not ':'

The NSP script joins DM_GAMES_DIR with os.pathsep (it puts a provisional or derived profile's folder
first), and patch_nso.py splits it the same way. game.py split it on ':', which is os.pathsep on
macOS and Linux but not on Windows, where the separator is ';' and ':' follows the drive letter.
On Windows "D:\Games\<id>_build\profile" became "D" and "\Games\<id>_build\profile", so a derived
profile (an update the profile does not register) was never found. Every tool silently used the
registered profile, and the build then stopped in report_profile_status with
KeyError: 'v1376256', because the registered profile has no build row for that version (Mario
Kart 8 Deluxe 3.0.x, built for the iOS shell from Windows).

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Windows builds of a derived or provisional profile used the registered profile and stopped with a KeyError
Issue: none yet (found building Mario Kart 8 Deluxe v1376256 on Windows, Zebuilder0/NX2Apple---Experiment claude/sharp-mayer-avybc7)
---
 dm/games/game.py | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/game.py b/dm/games/game.py
index cb28a9e..1c49803 100644
--- a/dm/games/game.py
+++ b/dm/games/game.py
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #   game.py modules <id> <folder of rewritten modules> (the modules to load from it: the build row of its main's build, else the profile's modules);
 #   game.py dir <id> (print the profile folder); game.py link <id> <link> (point a symlink at the profile folder: make cannot take paths with spaces)
 #   From Python: import game; g = game.load() (takes DM_GAME; there is no default game: unset is an error that lists the profiles); game.by_title(title ID); g.get / g.words / g.int / g.builds() / g.table(file name)
-# DM_GAMES_DIR (folders separated by ':') adds profile folders outside the repository, searched after dm/games: the NSP script writes a provisional profile for a game without one into
+# DM_GAMES_DIR (folders separated by os.pathsep: ':', ';' on Windows) adds profile folders outside the repository, searched after dm/games: the NSP script writes a provisional profile for a game without one into
 #   <NSP folder>/<id>_build/profile/<id>/ and points DM_GAMES_DIR at <id>_build/profile, so the shader tools, the host build and build_ipa.sh all find it.
 #   DM_GAMES_FIRST=1 searches DM_GAMES_DIR before dm/games (the NSP script's --provisional: a provisional profile for a game that has one in dm/games, to test the guesses)
 import os, re, sys
@@ -60,7 +60,8 @@ class Game:
 
 
 def extra_dirs():   # profile folders outside the repository (DM_GAMES_DIR), searched after dm/games
-    return [Path(p) for p in os.environ.get('DM_GAMES_DIR', '').split(':') if p]
+    # os.pathsep, as the NSP script and patch_nso.py write and read it: ':' split a Windows path at its drive letter
+    return [Path(p) for p in os.environ.get('DM_GAMES_DIR', '').split(os.pathsep) if p]
 
 
 def search_dirs():   # dm/games, then DM_GAMES_DIR; DM_GAMES_FIRST=1 the other way round
